OPTION H — Tabbed footer
=========================

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                         │
│  (tree content above)                                   │
│                                                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ┌Tools┐  Status   Help                                 │  ← tab strip
│  └─────┘                                                │
│  [+task] [zen] [explode] [📁]                           │  ← active tab body
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  [Boost] [██░ Claude] [██░ Codex]    [≡] [⚙]            │  ← persistent
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

TAB CONTENTS:
  Tools   → [+task] [zen] [explode] [📁]
  Status  → [agent●3] [panel] [⊟] [⬇]
  Help    → [trophy] [bar-chart] [handshake] [megaphone]
            [keyboard] [feedback]

· Persistent bottom = usage + view + settings (always seen)
· Tab body cycles between groups
· Settings = last
· Pros:  great organization, low icon count per view,
         users learn "Tools is workspace stuff"
· Cons:  extra click for non-active tab,
         contextual state hidden if not on Status tab,
         agent badge may need to bleed across tabs
